// Chapter 4 - Intune's Capabilities in Analytics and Automation
// From the book "AI, Automation and Analytics - Transforming Device Management
// with Intune" (2nd Edition) by Jannik Reinhard.
// https://github.com/JayRHa/intune-aaa-book-code
//
// Device Query is different from the Log Analytics KQL in kql-tutorial.kql: this
// KQL runs against a device's LIVE state, not a log workspace. Open a device in
// the Intune admin center, choose Device query, and paste one of these.
//
// Requires the Advanced Analytics license (folds into Microsoft 365 E3/E5 on
// 1 July 2026). Single-device limits: 128 KB payload, 15 queries/minute.

// Live CPU details from the selected device.
Cpu
| project ProcessorId, CurrentClockSpeed, MaxClockSpeed, CpuStatus

// Read a specific registry key.
WindowsRegistry('HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\\SOFTWARE\\...')
| project RegistryKey, ValueName, ValueType, ValueData

// System event-log entries from the last 7 days matching an event id.
WindowsEvent('System', 7d)
| where tostring(EventId) == '6008'
| project EventId, LoggedDateTime, LogName, Message, ProviderName
